\pard\sa40\fs28{\b Sylvester McDaniel Kollie}\par
\pard\sa200\cf2\fs18 sylvestermcdanielkollie@gmail.com  |  linkedin.com/in/sylvester-m  |  github.com/sylvester995  |  current-portfolio-nine.vercel.app\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 Hi ElevenLabs team,\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 I'm applying for your Full-Stack Engineer role. What made me want to write is that you judge engineers on what they've actually built rather than on titles or degrees, and that AI-first isn't a slogan for you - it's how the whole company works. That's exactly how I already build.\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 I founded AfriCarbon, a charcoal business in Liberia, and built its entire software stack myself with full ownership. The core of it, Charcoal Manager, is a product a real business runs on every day: a clean React and TypeScript front end over a Supabase/PostgreSQL backend, with REST APIs and authentication, shipped as an installable PWA on Vercel. It goes well beyond tracking - managing production, sales, and expenditure, projecting financials, guiding reinvestment decisions, and generating downloadable reports. I designed the UI, modeled the data, wrote the logic, and deployed it, end to end and solo.\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 AI is central to how I work. I use code assistants and AI APIs across my whole workflow to move faster at higher quality, but I treat their output as a first draft to be checked - verifying with tests and first-principles reasoning before anything ships. It's the same standard your "excellence everywhere" line describes: move fast, but let the quality match the work.\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 I care a lot about UI/UX - making powerful things feel intuitive - and the idea of building interfaces used by millions on top of your research team's models is genuinely exciting to me. I'm early in my career, but I take high ownership, I ship, and I learn fast. I'd love the chance to show you what I can build.\par
\pard\sa40\fs22 Thanks for your time,\par
\pard\sa0\fs22{\b Sylvester McDaniel Kollie}\par
